* Main shrine - Rebuilt with national funds in 1880.
* Inner worship hall and outer worship hall - Rebuilt in 1970.
* Noritoden - Rebuilt in 1970.
* Kojin Sapporo
* Jinko
* Shinbasha
* Shrine office
* Awarding place
* Okumiya Aihaisho
* Sanshuden
* {{ill|lt=campus|UNKNOWN|lt=large camphor}} - A sacred tree said to be over 1000 years old. Designated by Naruto City {{ill|lt=natural monument|Q23790|WD=Q23790|1=Natural monument}}.
* German Bridge - See "{{ill|lt=Deutsche Bridge|Q11322494|WD=Q11322494|1=German Bridge}}".
* Megane Bridge - Built by German soldiers who were imprisoned in {{ill|lt=Bando POW camp|Q324270|WD=Q324270|1=Bandō prisoner-of-war camp}} during the {{ill|UNKNOWN|lt=Taisho period|1=UNKNOWN}}.
* Otorii - You can see it when you pass by {{ill|lt=Reizanji (Naruto City)|Q1085463|WD=Q1085463|lt=Reizanji|1=Ryōzen-ji (Naruto)}} and go under the elevated {{ill|lt=Takamatsu Expressway|Q7677132|WD=Q7677132|1=Takamatsu Expressway}}. From here, a path lined with pine trees continues for about 800 meters. Rebuilt with steel pipes in 2002. Height: 14.6m.
* Okumiyamine Shrine - Enshrined at the top of Mt. Oasayama at an altitude of 538m. Climbing for about an hour and a half.
